# VS Code REST Client: run requests in order, one at a time.
# Start BE: cd D:\bookmg-workspace\bookmg-repo-be ; npm.cmd run dev
# After each write, rerun requests/readd-proof.sql in your MySQL client.
# OL45804W is Fantastic Mr. Fox. Use a different valid work ID if it is
# already on your shelf; do not delete an existing entry just for this demo.
# The work ID in the SQL file must match this workId.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@workId = OL45804W

### 1. Precondition: isInShelf must be false. If true, stop and choose another work ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### 2. First add: expect 201. DB: books=1, shelf_entries=1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}"
}

### 3. Duplicate while still on shelf: expect 409 BOOK_ALREADY_IN_SHELF.
### DB remains books=1, shelf_entries=1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}"
}

### 4. Remove from shelf: expect 200. DB: books=0, shelf_entries=0.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}

### 5. Membership is now false; neither table has this work ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### 6. Add again: expect 201, not 409. DB: new books=1, shelf_entries=1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}"
}

### 7. Duplicate again: expect 409. DB remains books=1, shelf_entries=1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}"
}

### Optional cleanup if the work was not on your shelf before step 1.
### This removes rows from both tables.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
